- Use the production Hivemind MCP environment only for Experiment ID uniqueness checks, final uniqueness rechecks, experiment creation, created experiment retrieval, and URL validation.
- Never use dev, staging, test, sandbox, local, preview, QA, or any non-production Hivemind environment for this setup workflow.
- If the production Hivemind environment cannot be verified before a Hivemind read or write, block and disclose the environment verification failure.
- Use Jira MCP for Jira retrieval and Jira link/comment writeback.
- Use Confluence MCP for linked documentation, shared mapping pages, and scorecard/metric library lookup when Jira data is insufficient.
- Do not use Helix in this workflow.
