## Edge cases
- Multiple channels -> derive primary from Jira or Confluence if clear; otherwise require user confirmation in preview.
- Missing campaign name -> show `REQUIRES USER INPUT` in preview, not upfront.
- Missing segment name -> show `REQUIRES USER INPUT` in preview, not upfront.
- Low-confidence segment recommendation -> mark `NEEDS CONFIRMATION` in preview.
- Missing hypothesis structure -> partial parse and flag gaps in preview.
- Missing Customer Problem -> mark separate Customer Problem field as `REQUIRES USER INPUT` in preview.
- Missing Experiment Theme -> mark Factor Change as `REQUIRES USER INPUT` in preview.
- Missing Calculator ID -> show `Not documented`, unless implementation requires it.
- Missing scorecard template or metrics -> derive from Confluence scorecard mapping library or mark required input in preview.
- Experiment Insights explicitly says `no insights`, `not based on prior research`, `no source`, or similar -> select `none`.
- Experiment Insights has no source after Jira and Confluence checks -> select `none`, confidence `Low`, and user action `Approve / Edit`.
- Experiment Insights references both a dashboard and a data analysis narrative -> choose `insights from business analytics` if analysis drove the hypothesis; choose `dashboard` if the dashboard itself is the cited source.
- Experiment Insights references FullStory and customer interviews -> choose the source most directly tied to the hypothesis. If unclear, choose `customer research` only when interview or research findings are primary; otherwise choose `full story`.
- Experiment Insights references a prior Hivemind experiment plus any other source -> select `hivemind experiment` unless the ticket clearly states the other source is the primary basis.
- Experiment Insights source is a stakeholder request with no analytics, research, replay, or prior experiment evidence -> select `other` and describe the stakeholder or business source.
- Conflicting Jira fields -> prioritize Hypothesis > Experiment Theme > Summary, and disclose conflict in preview.
- Missing required fields after preview -> block creation until resolved during review.
- Invalid naming inputs -> sanitize and show cleanup applied.
- Existing Hivemind link -> ask before overwrite and use comment/remote link fallback if needed.
- Jira customfield_34621 update succeeds but read-back does not show the production Hivemind URL -> block final success and retry or request explicit fallback approval.
- Jira customfield_34621 is not writable -> disclose, do not claim field update success, and use comment/remote link only after explicit user fallback approval.
- Selected scorecard template contains informative metrics -> include all informative metrics in preview and creation payload unless explicitly excluded by user.
- Selected scorecard template metadata cannot be retrieved -> disclose and require explicit user approval before creating without template informative metrics.
- Base Experiment ID already exists in Hivemind -> append `_1`, then `_2`, then `_3`, etc. until unique.
- Suffixed Experiment ID already exists in Hivemind -> continue incrementing until unique.
- Hivemind uniqueness lookup unavailable -> block creation and report a blocking error.
- Race condition where Final Experiment ID becomes taken after approval but before creation -> re-run suffix resolution and report the updated Final Experiment ID.
- Hivemind MCP target points to dev, staging, test, sandbox, local, preview, QA, or another non-production environment -> block creation and do not link Jira.
- Hivemind experiment is accidentally created in a non-production environment -> disclose, do not link Jira, and retry only after production target is verified.

